The optional on-device summary feature downloads and runs
onnx-community/t5-cnn-25k-ONNX, revision
c8ac103cd6b1937ba0f6c5d4bcc9eb18d8e19c95, through Transformers.js and ONNX
Runtime Web. Its tokenizer is loaded from google-t5/t5-small, revision

df1b051c49625cf57a3d0d8d3863ed4d13564fe4.

Both model repositories identify their models as Apache-2.0 licensed. The T5
CNN model card describes it as T5-small fine-tuned on CNN/DailyMail for
abstractive summarization. See:
https://huggingface.co/onnx-community/t5-cnn-25k-ONNX/tree/c8ac103cd6b1937ba0f6c5d4bcc9eb18d8e19c95
https://huggingface.co/google-t5/t5-small/tree/df1b051c49625cf57a3d0d8d3863ed4d13564fe4

The model is loaded only after the owner explicitly requests an on-device
summary. Transcript text stays on the device. Model assets are fetched from
the revision-pinned public model repositories and their allowlisted CDN
redirects.
